x86_64-linux  three recorded shapes: the C1/D1 forms of the in-class members; the placement pair declared for the oracle's sake, `_ZnwmPv` and `_ZdlPvS_`, emitted where clang elides them; and clang's `_Unwind_Resume` with the personality reference, a cleanup freeing the storage should a constructor throw in `new Der`, which cxx1 does not build for a new-expression (operator-new.nonames). The allocation and deallocation names agree - `??2`/`??3` of Base and Der, `_ZN4BasenwEm` and the rest.
x86_64-windows  the placement pair once more, and `??1Plain@@QEAA@XZ`, a destructor cl inlines away; every other name agrees.
arm64-darwin  the same three.
